            {
              "block_label": "table",
              "block_content": "<table><tr><td>Feature</td><td>Collection methods on MRI</td></tr><tr><td>Tendon diseases classification</td><td>No tears, tendinopathy without tears, partial tears and full-thickness tears.</td></tr><tr><td>Acromial spurs classification</td><td>Type I, flat; type II, curved; type III, hooked; type IV, convex.</td></tr><tr><td>Inferior glenohumeral distance</td><td>The distance of the inferior glenoid margin and the inferior humeral head margin (intersection of the humeral head articular margin and the humeral neck).</td></tr><tr><td>Critical shoulder angle Supraspi natus tendon thickness</td><td>Measured between a line connecting the inferior with the superior border of the glenoid fossa and another connecting the inferior border of the glenoid with the most inferolateral point of the acromion.</td></tr><tr><td>Coracoac romial ligament status</td><td>Whether there were a thickened coracoacromial ligament and acromioclavicular enthesophytes.</td></tr><tr><td>Acromial angle</td><td>The angle between the line drawn along the lower surface of the acromion and the horizontal line was measured. The scapular axis was drawn from most medial aspect of the scapula body to the centre of the glenoid fossa in axial position, and a glenoid line was drawn connecting the anterior and posterior margins of the glenoid fossa. The glenoid version angle was measured as the angle between the glenoid line and the line perpendicular to the scapular axis.</td></tr><tr><td>Glenoid version angle</td><td>Using a sagittal MRI image, and the most lateral slice in which the scapular spine was seen in contact with the scapular body. The tangent sign was considered positive when the supraspinatus muscle did not cross the tangent.</td></tr><tr><td>Supraspi natus tangent sign</td><td>In the same MRI slice used for the tangent sign, by measuring the area under the tangent sign and limited by the scapular spine and the coracoid, the cross-sectional area of the supraspinatus muscle was then measured and presented as an occupation ratio of area of the supraspinatus muscle divided by the overall area under the tangent in the supraspinatus fossa.</td></tr><tr><td>Occupation grade</td><td>The angle between the line drawn along the lower surface of the acromion and the horizontal line was measured. The scapular axis was drawn from most medial aspect of the scapula body to the centre of the glenoid fossa in axial position, and a glenoid line was drawn connecting the anterior and posterior margins of the glenoid fossa. The glenoid version angle was measured as the angle between the glenoid line and the line perpendicular to the scapular axis.</td></tr></table>",
